WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.077 --> 00:00:04.244
(school bell ringing)

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.370
- Happy Friday Crete leaders!

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:10.770
I'd like to first thank everyone
for an awesome week back.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.920
I've seen some amazing things.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.010
Not only are students embodying
the Crete core values,

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.820
but I saw rockets being made

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.540
and launching in the steam class.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.560
I saw critical thinking and reasoning

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.390
going on in the chess class.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.910
And I saw students
dancing their hearts out

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.250
in the dance class.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.930
So great job during enrichment.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.960
Great job this first week back.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.430
Keep it up and keep embodying
the Crete core values.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.240
I hope you all have a wonderful week.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.980
I will see you on the yard.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.053
And as always, cheerio.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.720
- What's six times four?

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:56.900
24.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.409
All right?

00:00:58.409 --> 00:00:59.989
- One.

00:00:59.989 --> 00:01:01.637
Good.

00:01:01.637 --> 00:01:03.475
Can you show me now?

00:01:03.475 --> 00:01:05.600
You have to test brands.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.637
- How do you say that word again?

00:01:06.637 --> 00:01:08.035
- Perserverence.

00:01:08.035 --> 00:01:09.353
- What's the next one?

00:01:09.353 --> 00:01:10.186
- Respect.

00:01:10.186 --> 00:01:11.114
- And what's our last one?

00:01:11.114 --> 00:01:12.249
- Vision.

00:01:12.249 --> 00:01:13.082
- You are dismissed.

00:01:13.082 --> 00:01:14.790
- Crete Academy is a
non-profit charter school

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:17.120
serving students pre-K through sixth grade

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.420
in South Los Angeles who are experiencing

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.393
homelessness and extreme poverty.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:26.600
Of the 187 students we are 20% special ed.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.430
We are 85 percent free and reduced lunch,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.120
meaning living below the poverty line.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.130
And we are 30 percent
homeless, meaning students

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.960
living in shelters, motels, hotels,

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.883
and double and tripled
up with family members.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:48.030
I decided to open this school 15 years ago

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:51.580
when I was volunteering
as a freshman in college

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:52.970
downtown on Skid Row.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:56.270
And seeing thousands and
thousands of people living

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:01.270
in boxes and under tarps
and in sleeping bags.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.640
I knew then that I wanted to do something,

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.760
and I felt that the answer
was a good education.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:13.250
And creating a space where
these unique children,

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.150
because they are unique
in their situations,

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.113
could come and thrive.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.870
I chose to start this
school in South Central

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.490
because it's known for violence,

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:29.140
high poverty rates, and low
educational attainment rates.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.230
Kids who come through
those doors every day

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.770
in these public schools
are lacking basic needs.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.403
And I want to see that change.

00:02:40.813 --> 00:02:44.240
- In my old school all
the classrooms were dirty.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.113
There was holes in the walls.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:50.010
And they didn't really care for us.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.963
Most of the kids got in fights a lot.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.150
- At my old school I was
just getting in trouble

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.820
just for doing a lot of

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.780
weird stuff and hanging
around with the wrong people.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.670
- Some kids were getting all over me

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.480
and one of the staff was just watching,

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.363
and I was right in front
of her and she did nothing.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.780
This school has really helped me

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.870
get through so many tough times.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.710
- [Je'ky] They have a lot of smart people

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:19.840
that make smart choices,

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.180
and I hang around with them now.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.253
- [Naya] This school is
like my dream school.

00:03:37.392 --> 00:03:38.883
- Good morning.

00:03:38.883 --> 00:03:39.716
Come on.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.150
- [Camilla] Without transportation many

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.900
of the kids would not go to school.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.500
So one of the things that we provide

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.540
at our school that's critical

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.630
to our students' success
and overall family support

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.040
is our transportation.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.775
We transport 59 students
every day to school

00:04:00.775 --> 00:04:04.780
using two shuttle buses that
each take on two routes.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.263
So starting at 5:30.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.380
By providing transportation
we're alleviating

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.890
some of the burden on our families

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.460
and really creating more opportunity

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.053
for them to have one less
thing to worry about.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:21.108
- Pound, we pounding this morning?

00:04:21.108 --> 00:04:22.060
Pew.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.013
You want breakfast?

00:04:23.013 --> 00:04:24.249
- [Camilla] When a student first arrives

00:04:24.249 --> 00:04:25.220
in the morning at Crete,

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.830
they're greeted by our Dean of Students

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.020
who usually stands at the front gate.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.800
And, majority, 90 percent of the students

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.503
will come and get breakfast.

00:04:38.483 --> 00:04:40.158
- [Woman] Good morning.

00:04:40.158 --> 00:04:42.228
So how's your day today?

00:04:42.228 --> 00:04:43.061
- Good.

00:04:43.061 --> 00:04:43.894
- You good?

00:04:43.894 --> 00:04:45.240
That's all I want to know.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.270
- [Camilla] We first of all understand

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.061
that there are basic
needs that must be met

00:04:50.061 --> 00:04:52.670
before we can educate our kids.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:55.860
Before we put math or
science or social studies,

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.290
before you, we want to
make sure that your mind,

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.800
your body, and everything else is intact.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.870
So we offer three meals a day.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:06.457
We offer mental health resources through

00:05:06.457 --> 00:05:11.010
our wellness program so on-site
social workers full time.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.250
All the things that you would need

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.443
just to be a healthy human.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.340
- I didn't have a car the first
year that Crete opened up.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.660
But the school made sure my kids were

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:28.660
on the shuttle and they never
missed school because of that.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.320
I'm a single mom.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.210
I was married for seven years,

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:36.023
and I left due to domestic violence.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.520
Being in the shelter and being

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:44.250
in this space in my life
where I'm currently homeless,

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.980
it kind of eases you know,

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.900
my thinking process like,
OK, my kids are safe.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.470
I don't have to worry about that.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:54.333
Now let me go and try to
do this, try to do that.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:59.720
It takes the stress off a bit
knowing that my kids are okay.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.150
- [Camilla] I've always
wanted it to be more

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:12.620
than just a school, and I'm
proud and excited for where

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:15.513
we're at, but there's so
much more that I want to do.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.140
The highlight of working here

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.020
is always seeing the kids smile.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.470
I know every kids' story.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:27.560
I get to know them very
deeply and intimately.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.010
I know their family stories.

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:33.350
And so to know where they're coming from

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:36.040
and what they've been
through, and to see them

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.440
run around on the playground, or you know

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.810
show me their book report or
their science fair project,

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:43.327
that's what gets me every day.

00:06:44.202 --> 00:06:45.820
Every time, it's what
wakes me up in the morning.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:49.370
Is to see that despite
those circumstances,

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:51.820
despite where you came from

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.590
and what you might be going through now,

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:55.423
you can smile.

00:06:56.707 --> 00:06:57.790
There's hope.

00:07:00.051 --> 00:07:02.968
(orchestral music)

